    "result_text": "All green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing. The audit output confirms the behavior end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What changed\n\n**Version-2 region code inside identifiers** (`OwnerRegion.java`)\n- `of(...)` still returns the plain region (`NSW`) \u2014 this feeds `locality`, `timezone`, and the segment classification.\n- New `identityRegion(...)` = `\"V2\" + plainRegion` (e.g. `V2NSW`). This tagged region is the single ingredient threaded into all three identifiers, so every one changes and can never reproduce a v1 value (v1 regions are `NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN`; v2 always starts with `V2`). Added `OwnerFieldsDto` overloads so the request-side duplicate check derives the same region.\n\n**Identifiers rederived**\n- `AssignMemberId` \u2014 `memberId` prefix is now the v2 region \u2192 `V2NSW271A2B3C4D6`.\n- `HouseholdId.derive(...)` \u2014 now hashes `identityRegion|lastName|postcode`.\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.build(...)` \u2014 now hashes `v2Region|telephone|email|soundex`; both request and existing owners derive symmetrically, so duplicate detection stays consistent.\n\n**Owner segment recomputed from the v2 identity** (`OwnerSegment.java`)\n- Derives its region via `OwnerRegion.segmentRegion(owner)` \u2014 the identity region with the `V2` tag stripped \u2014 so it sources from the v2 identity yet keeps a plain region (no `V2` leak).\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`)\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`.\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a nested `identity` object; the three top-level fields are removed. Mapper populates it via a `toIdentity(owner)` helper.\n- Updated `locality` docs to reflect it's the plain region without the tag.\n\n**Audit schema v2** (`AuditOwnerCreated.java`)\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` gains a fixed `schemaVersion: 2` (shape `{schemaVersion, seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, event}`); the `memberId` it records is the v2 value.\n\nRequest fields are untouched.",
