    "probe_text": "Here is what actually executes when you `POST /api/owners`, in order.\n\n## Which path is live\n\nThe **OfficeFloor YAML pipeline** handles this request \u2014 not a Spring MVC controller. There are no `@RestController`/`@PostMapping` classes in the source at all, and the required starter (`officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter`) *is* present in `pom.xml`, so the YAML under `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` is active (contrary to the \"inert without the starter\" caveat \u2014 the starter is there).\n\nOne consequence worth flagging up front: the request binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` **without `@Valid`**, so the bean-validation annotations on `OwnerFieldsDto` (and on the `Owner`/`Person` entity) are effectively inert. All enforcement is done by explicit pipeline steps.\n\n## Guard (before anything runs)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n## Idempotency gate\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads only the `Idempotency-Key` header. If the key was already used for a prior successful create \u2192 short-circuits to **RespondWithExistingOwner** (replays the original owner, **HTTP 200**, `readonly-transaction`). Otherwise continues.\n\n## Validations / normalizations (operate on the DTO, before the entity is built)\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerRequiredFields** \u2014 binds the body; normalizes address (prefers `addressLine1`+`addressLine2`, falls back to flat `address`); rejects blank `firstName`, `lastName`, composed `address`, `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n3. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 if supplied and after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n4. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts to E.164 (default country code `+61`); invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). *(mutates in place)*\n5. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 optional; must match email regex else `InvalidEmailException`; trims + lowercases. *(mutates in place)*\n6. **ValidateOwnerEmailDomain** \u2014 optional; rejects disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n7. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 optional; must be 4 digits and within the city's region range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n8. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold==true`, SHA-256 identity key (telephone|email|soundex(lastName)); collision with a non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409).\n9. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 city already holding \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n10. **EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** \u2014 rolls to a business day; \u2265 100 owners that day \u2192 `TooManyOwnersTodayException` (429).\n\n## Build + enrichment (side-effects \u2014 all under `govern: [ transaction ]`, on the `Owner` entity)\n\n11. **BuildOwner** \u2014 MapStruct maps DTO \u2192 new `Owner` (id/pets ignored); transaction begins here.\n12. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 over region/lastName/postcode).\n13. **AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 count of owners sharing `householdId` + 1.\n14. **ApplyRegistrationDate** \u2014 sets effective registration date (supplied or today), rolled off weekends/holidays.\n15. **AssignMemberId** \u2014 `<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn>`, de-duplicated with `-<n>` on collision.\n16. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 count of pre-existing same first+last name owners.\n17. **AssignMembershipLevel** \u2014 computes `membershipPoints` (email +2, no namesakes +1, household \u22653 +2, tenure >1 FY +3) \u2192 derived `membershipLevel` (1\u20134).\n18. **CapMembershipLevel** \u2014 caps level at (max household member's level + 1).\n19. **AssignBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning` = (>80 owners that business day).\n20. **AssignCapacityWarning** \u2014 `capacityWarning` = (city count in 40\u201349).\n21. **AssignPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 soft-match flag (same soundex(lastName)+postcode, differing identity key); skipped if `sharesHousehold` or no postcode.\n\n## Persistence + post-commit side-effects (still in the transaction)\n\n22. **SaveOwner** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (assigns id).\n23. **RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 if header present, records key \u2192 owner id.\n24. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 logs human-readable line + structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event (schemaVersion 2, monotonic seq) via `AUDIT` logger.\n25. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** \u2014 logs welcome message via `NOTIFY` logger.\n26. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (enriched: selfLink, salutation, displayName, initials, locality, timezone, contactPreference, apiVersion=2, identity, ageBand, ownerSegment, fiscalYear, telephoneDisplay, riskFlag); sends **HTTP 201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Two things to keep in mind:** (1) the DTO/entity bean-validation annotations (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`, `Person`'s `@NotEmpty`, etc.) do **not** run here \u2014 the body is bound without `@Valid`, so validation is only whatever steps 2\u201310 do explicitly. (2) The whole enrichment-through-response sequence runs inside one transaction that commits at the end.\n\nWant me to double-check any specific step (e.g. the exact fields validated, or the DTO annotations) against the source?"
